Cell["\<\
As one can see in the symbolic delta product array, we are adding three new \
indices, 1->2, 2->2, and 3->2 (replacing the index 2 that was shared by 3 \
tensors)\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.977580817636264*^9, 3.9775808746531353`*^9}, {
  3.97758227378633*^9, 
  3.977582287700655*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8174287b-2f9c-4fa3-93d9-\
52f6b5cd5698"],

Cell["\<\
Since graph is always binary, if one asks for Graph of a TN, one gets \
automatically a spider (symbolic delta-product tensor) added. Note that in \
the graph, the vertices are tensors and edges are contraction indices between \
tensors/vertices while free indices are not shown:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9760689310800047`*^9, 3.976068980944517*^9}, {
  3.977582388228795*^9, 3.977582403086128*^9}, {3.977582450290236*^9, 
  3.977582492547123*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ac2bbf7f-d0f0-43b2-b9a5-\
8000b39cc581"],

