Cell["\<\
This is the best performance using inactive TensorContract and inactive \
TensorProduct, with global contraction indices.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.977662517692528*^9, 
  3.977662542964952*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"79d45929-295d-4929-99de-\
2c2dc89bd470"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["TensorNetworkFindContractionPath", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.976071502187851*^9},ExpressionUUID->"e35a300f-7f8c-4057-9aa6-\
cb3ad44470b3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Finds an optimized contraction path using the ",
 ButtonBox["Cotengra library",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://cotengra.readthedocs.io/en/latest/"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://cotengra.readthedocs.io/en/latest/"],
 ".\n- ",
 StyleBox["Optimal",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": means an exhaustive (depth-first) search that will find the best path for \
the chosen objective, but it\[CloseCurlyQuote]s slow and only practical for \
smaller problems.\n\nThese are different cost functions you can ask the \
optimizer to minimize:\n- ",
 StyleBox["flops",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": minimize the total number of scalar operations (classic \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]fastest compute\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] proxy).\n- ",
 StyleBox["size",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": minimize the largest intermediate tensor (a proxy for peak memory / \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]contraction width\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]).\n- ",
 StyleBox["max",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": minimize the single most expensive contraction step (the worst per-step \
asymptotic scaling).\n- ",
 StyleBox["write",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": minimize the total size of all intermediates created (roughly, how much \
memory gets written / potentially stored\[LongDash]often relevant for \
autodiff).\n- ",
 StyleBox["combo",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": minimize flops + \[Alpha] x write (summed over contractions). This tries \
to balance compute vs memory bandwidth; default \[Alpha]=64 in these \
implementations.\n- ",
 StyleBox["limit",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": minimize max(flops, \[Alpha] x write) (summed over contractions), again \
typically with default \[Alpha]=64. This penalizes steps that are either very \
compute-heavy or very memory-heavy, encouraging more \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]balanced\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] steps..\n"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.976075763503169*^9, 3.976075806234371*^9}, 
   3.9761184401044683`*^9, {3.976138401409347*^9, 3.9761384486475267`*^9}, 
   3.976138481989006*^9, {3.977582584595129*^9, 3.977582584595777*^9}, {
   3.977584341795038*^9, 3.9775844142913647`*^9}, {3.977584452319601*^9, 
   3.977584499252531*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0d6ab6d9-c98f-4653-8a47-\
b0e58680dfa2"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"paths", "=", 
  RowBox[{"AssociationMap", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"TensorNetworkFindContractionPath", "[", 
      RowBox[{"tn2", ",", 
       RowBox[{"Method", "->", "#"}]}], "]"}], "&"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Optimal\>\"", ",", "\"\<flops\>\"", ",", "\"\<max\>\"", 
      ",", "\"\<size\>\"", ",", "\"\<write\>\"", ",", "\"\<combo\>\"", 
      ",", "\"\<limit\>\""}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.976070919293901*^9, 3.976070933468061*^9}, {
